---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import { site, socials } from '@/lib/site';
import { href } from '@/lib/paths';
import { roles, principles } from '@/data/experience';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

const title = 'About';
const description =
  'Samuel Mussie — co-founder and CTO of Mereb Technologies in Addis Ababa. A decade of shipping software, five years building the engineering organisation behind it.';
---

<Layout {title} {description} path="/about" type="profile">
  <!-- ── Header ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 grid-lines opacity-60" aria-hidden="true">
    </div>
    <div class="wrap relative py-16 lg:py-24">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>02 &nbsp;About</p>
      <div class="mt-7 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7">
          <h1
            class="display text-[clamp(2.4rem,6.6vw,4.25rem)]"
            data-reveal
            style="--reveal-delay:60ms"
          >
            Ten years of code. Five of them<br class="hidden lg:block" />
            <em class="italic text-accent">answering for other people’s.</em>
          </h1>
        </div>
        <div class="lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9 lg:pt-3">
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-muted" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
            I write less code than I used to and think about hiring more than about architecture.
            That was the correct trade, and it took me a year to stop resenting it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Narrative ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="wrap py-16 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="prose" data-reveal>
          <p>
            I’m Samuel Mussie. I co-founded <a
              href={site.companyUrl}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Mereb Technologies</a
            > and I run engineering there — the hiring bar, the delivery model, and the architecture decisions
            behind every team we place.
          </p>
          <p>
            The short version of what we do: we give SaaS companies in Europe and the US dedicated
            senior engineering teams, contracted through an EU entity, delivered from Addis Ababa.
            The teams work inside the client’s process, on the client’s board, in the client’s
            codebase. From the outside it looks like an in-house hire. That is the point.
          </p>

          <h2>How this started</h2>
          <p>
            Before Mereb was a company it was a handful of us in Addis Ababa taking contracts
            individually. Node and Python services, React front ends, iOS and Flutter apps, a few
            Telegram bots that solved distinctly Ethiopian problems. Good work, no shortage of it.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 2021 we stopped doing that and built a company instead, because freelancing has a
            ceiling and it sits in three specific places: you cannot bid on the two-year embedded
            engagements that are the most interesting work; you cannot say no in a way that means
            anything; and you cannot build a quality bar that survives you.
          </p>
          <p>
            That last one is what decided it. Individually, quality is a fact about you.
            Collectively, it has to become something written, teachable and enforceable — or it
            regresses to the mean of whoever you hired last.
          </p>

          <h2>What the job actually is</h2>
          <p>
            Mostly writing, which I did not expect. A distributed engineering organisation running
            across six time zones is functionally a writing organisation: the decisions that survive
            are the written ones, and the engineers who compound fastest are the ones who explain
            themselves well.
          </p>
          <p>The rest of it comes down to three things I hold strictly:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>The bar is not negotiable.</strong> Six-plus years of production experience, and
              no juniors on client work. That policy has cost us deals, which is how I know it is a policy
              and not a page on a website.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Continuity is an architecture problem.</strong> After six months inside a client’s
              system, an engineer knows which service has the undocumented retry and why a table has a
              nullable column that should never be null. None of that is in the repository. Rotating them
              out deletes it, so retention is something I design around.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The reference call is the product.</strong> Nobody in Berlin buys an Ethiopian engineering
              team from a website. They buy it because another CTO told them it worked — which makes every
              engagement a sales asset or a liability, with no third category.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Where I still get my hands dirty</h2>
          <p>
            Enough to have opinions I can defend. I built a full retrieval-augmented chat system end
            to end before advising a single client on an AI feature, because I refuse to advise from
            blog posts. I wrote a Flutter chat app in 2019 and a native Swift app in 2020 so that my
            answer on cross-platform tradeoffs comes from having shipped both, with the same feature
            set, eighteen months apart.
          </p>
          <p>
            The side projects are the same instinct. Fantasy Premier League tooling I use every
            week, a Jeopardy game for team nights, a URL shortener built twice to see what the
            second attempt taught me. If a pattern survives a Saturday when everyone opens the app
            at once, it is probably ready for someone’s production.
          </p>

          <h2>The thing underneath all of it</h2>
          <p>
            In 2020 I built a Telegram bot that <em>tried</em> to translate text into Amharic. I have
            never edited that word out of the repository description, because it was accurate and it dates
            a position I still hold: the AI capability gap for African languages is a data and incentive
            problem, not a model problem.
          </p>
          <p>
            Which is the same sentence I end up writing about most things. There is no shortage of
            engineers in this city who could close that gap, or hold their own on any team in
            Europe. There is a shortage of companies who have looked.
          </p>
          <p>Mereb is my argument that the looking is worth it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Sidebar -->
      <aside class="lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9">
        <div class="sticky top-24 space-y-8" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:80ms">
          <div class="card rounded-lg p-6">
            <h2 class="font-mono text-2xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-subtle">At a glance</h2>
            <dl class="mt-5 space-y-3.5 text-sm">
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Role</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">{site.role}</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Company</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">
                  <a href={site.companyUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link"
                    >Mereb Technologies</a
                  >
                </dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Based in</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">Addis Ababa, ET</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Studied at</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">Addis Ababa University</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Languages</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">Amharic, English</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
                <dt class="text-subtle">Timezone</dt>
                <dd class="text-right text-fg">EAT / GMT+3</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
            <div class="rule my-5"></div>
            <ul class="space-y-2.5">
              {
                socials.map((s) => (
                  <li>
                    <a
                      href={s.href}
                      target={s.href.startsWith('http') ? '_blank' : undefined}
                      rel={s.href.startsWith('http') ? 'noopener noreferrer me' : undefined}
                      class="group flex items-center justify-between gap-3 text-sm text-muted transition-colors hover:text-fg"
                    >
                      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                        <Icon name={s.icon} class="size-3.5 opacity-70" aria-hidden="true" />
                        {s.label}
                      </span>
                      <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-subtle group-hover:text-accent">
                        {s.handle}
                      </span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="card rounded-lg p-6">
            <h2 class="font-mono text-2xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-subtle">
              Beyond the desk
            </h2>
            <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
              <li>
                Fantasy Premier League, seriously enough to have <a
                  href={href('/work/fantasy-pl')}
                  class="link">built tooling for it</a
                >.
              </li>
              <li>
                The <a href={site.companyUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link"
                  >Mereb Podcast</a
                > — our Amharic-language show putting Ethiopian engineers and founders on record.
              </li>
              <li>Advent of Code every December, in Python, badly, happily.</li>
              <li>Arguing that PHP runs more of the world than anyone admits.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Timeline ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section
    index="05"
    eyebrow="Timeline"
    title="Where the time went."
    lede="Anything I cannot verify publicly is left general rather than dressed up. If you need exact dates for a due-diligence process, ask and I will send them."
    id="timeline"
  >
    <ol class="space-y-px overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-line bg-line">
      {
        roles.map((role, i) => (
          <li class="bg-surface p-7 lg:p-9" data-reveal style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 80}ms`}>
            <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-8">
              <div class="lg:col-span-3">
                <p class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-2xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-subtle">
                  {role.from && role.to ? `${role.from} — ${role.to}` : 'Earlier'}
                  {role.current && (
                    <span class="relative flex size-1.5">
                      <span class="absolute inline-flex size-full animate-ping rounded-full bg-jade opacity-70" />
                      <span class="relative inline-flex size-1.5 rounded-full bg-jade" />
                    </span>
                  )}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-[0.8125rem] leading-snug text-subtle">{role.location}</p>
              </div>

              <div class="lg:col-span-9">
                <h3 class="text-xl font-medium tracking-tight lg:text-[1.375rem]">{role.title}</h3>
                <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-accent">
                  {role.url ? (
                    <a
                      href={role.url}
                      target="_blank"
                      rel="noopener noreferrer"
                      class="link link-accent"
                    >
                      {role.org}
                    </a>
                  ) : (
                    role.org
                  )}
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
                  {role.summary}
                </p>
                {role.highlights.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="mt-5 space-y-2.5">
                    {role.highlights.map((h) => (
                      <li class="relative max-w-2xl pl-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">
                        <span
                          class="absolute left-0 top-[0.72em] h-px w-2.5 bg-accent"
                          aria-hidden="true"
                        />
                        {h}
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}
                {role.tags.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5" aria-label="Focus areas">
                    {role.tags.map((t) => (
                      <li class="chip">{t}</li>
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </Section>

  <!-- ── Principles ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <Section
    index="06"
    eyebrow="Positions"
    title="What I will argue about."
    lede="Each of these has cost us something at least once. That is the test."
  >
    <div class="grid gap-x-10 gap-y-12 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        principles.map((p, i) => (
          <div class="border-t border-line pt-6" data-reveal style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 70}ms`}>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <Icon name={p.icon} class="size-4 text-accent" aria-hidden="true" />
              <h3 class="text-[1.0625rem] font-medium tracking-tight">{p.title}</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3.5 max-w-lg text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-muted">{p.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
